## 1. Overview & Problem Definition

Phase H implements the **Heatwave and Data-Dependent Severe-Wind Reliability Specialist (`HEATWAVE_RELIABILITY_V1`)**, addressing extreme heat spells, severe thermal departures, tropical warm nights, and convective severe wind gusts across India.
In accordance with Veyra's non-negotiable architectural principles:
- Reliability is never collapsed into an opaque composite score.
- Decomposes failure into:
  1. Heatwave occurrence threshold exceedance (`HEATWAVE-THRESH-01`, $T_{max} \ge 40.0^\circ\text{C}$ & departure $\ge 4.5^\circ\text{C}$ in plains; $37^\circ\text{C}$ coastal; $30^\circ\text{C}$ hills).
  2. Peak maximum temperature absolute error exceedance (`HEATWAVE-PEAK-01`, $|T_{max}^{fc} - T_{max}^{obs}| > 2.5^\circ\text{C}$).
  3. Heatwave spell onset timing error exceedance (`HEATWAVE-ONSET-01`, onset offset $> 24.0$h).
  4. Spell duration and persistence error exceedance (`HEATWAVE-DURATION-01`, duration error $> 48.0$h / 2 days).
  5. Warm night minimum temperature departure error exceedance (`HEATWAVE-NIGHT-01`, $|T_{min}^{fc} - T_{min}^{obs}| > 2.0^\circ\text{C}$ when $T_{max} \ge 40.0^\circ\text{C}$).
  6. Spatial extent area coverage fraction error exceedance (`HEATWAVE-SPATIAL-01`, area fraction error $> 0.20$).
  7. Severe wind gale gust error exceedance (`WIND-GUST-THRESH-01`, $|V_{fc} - V_{obs}| > 6.0$ m/s on gusts $\ge 17.2$ m/s).
- Severe wind evaluation is data-dependent: strictly conditional on paired forecast/reference observations, otherwise explicitly `null`.
- Anti-leakage at $t_0$: only issue-time atmospheric state enters inference; verification data sealed with 24h verification latency.
- Full Level 1-4 baseline ladder comparison.

